To answer the question, we can use the `Object_Detector_Tool` tool. Here's the Python code to execute the tool and get the result:

```python
from object_detector import Object_Detector_Tool

# The image file path provided in the code
image_path = "/path/to/image.png"

# Label to detect
labels = ["baseball", "basket"]

# Default confidence threshold (0.35), use the available threshold provided in the tool documentation
threshold = 0.35

# Model size
model_size = "tiny"

# Path to save the detected object images
saved_object_path = "detected_objects"

# Execute the tool
result = Object_Detector_Tool.execute(image=image_path, labels=labels, save_object=True, thresholds=[threshold], model_size=model_size, saved_image_path=saved_object_path)

# Get the result
detected_objects = result[0]
total_objects = result[1]

# Print the result
print(detected_objects)
print("Detected objects:", total_objects)
```

Make sure to replace `/path/to/image.png` with the actual path to the image file you've provided.
